    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d507">

                <pb facs="0614" n="356" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg356"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 300.115/2585</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-30">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 30, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1342. Your 1789, 15th.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d507-f1"/> Have consignments actually
                    been placed in prize court? If so, report date and reasons assigned. If not,
                    Inform Foreign Office owners protest and request release on ground goods were
                    shipped in neutral trade between neutral countries and were not contraband.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
